			<div class="content" id="post-content-4469314">
									

<p>I&#8230; disagree with this disagreement. To me this implies people should judge a -000 contest entry as they would judge any other article, and hold it to identical standards. If you want to approach it in this way, that's fine, but I have no hesitation in saying that I sometimes vote differently on contest entries than I would otherwise if they were normally posted, and I'm pretty sure I'm not alone in this - there's nothing wrong with having a differing set of expectations for what are supposed to be important articles for the site.</p>
<p>With regards to the article itself, it was strong in parts - it held my attention through to the first addendum, and the overall idea has potential - but I wasn't a fan for a few reasons, most of which gee0765 went through with regards to the length, ending and pacing. I didn't really care for the part you spoilered in the author post - I didn't notice it as I couldn't see the hidden text on mobile, but when I found out my reaction was &quot;ok, so?&quot; because it didn't seem to change the meaning or 'feel' of the vast majority of the article - which is fine to have this hidden secret as an 'easter egg', but not great if you wanted it to be a central part of the mystery.</p>
<p>The X-men thing has come up in the above comments. I would add that it was jarring with the tone of the article - maybe if there was some humour in it, but you've clearly tried to go for a serious take on serious real life issues of oppression and injustice, which is also fine, but I couldn't personally get past this being a motley band of misfits granted powers by nature to fight evildoers. It's serious Captain Planet which is kind of a contradiction in terms.</p>
<p>I also found the sudden change of heart in the last log to stretch plausibility to the extent that I had to reread thinking that I'd missed them being either a) old friends or b) mind influencing powers were involved but he really did just flip after 5 lines of convincing.</p>

